From: Mihawk <163614687+mihawk-99@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] advapi32: PS5: the Windows user is Mihawk, not Proton's steamuser

Proton answers GetUserNameA/W with a fixed "steamuser" whatever the Unix user is, and every profile path Wine makes
follows from it: shell32 expands %USERPROFILE% to C:\users\<GetUserNameW> (so the known folders, Documents, AppData,
Saved Games), wineboot records it as the ProfileList ProfileImagePath and the Volatile Environment's USERPROFILE and
USERNAME, and LookupAccountSid names the first user by it. Mihawk OS's user is Mihawk, so the fixed name is Mihawk.
Prefixes made before (v2.0.0-alpha-1 and -2, C:\users\steamuser with the users' saves) are moved to the new name by
the title before Wine starts on them (src/pw_wine_profile.h), which leaves C:\users\steamuser as a link to the new
folder for programs that stored the old absolute path.
---
--- a/dlls/advapi32/advapi.c
+++ b/dlls/advapi32/advapi.c
@@ -44,7 +44,8 @@
  */
 BOOL WINAPI GetUserNameA( LPSTR name, LPDWORD size )
 {
-    static const char steamuserA[] = {'s','t','e','a','m','u','s','e','r',0};
+    /* PS5: Mihawk OS's user; its profile is C:\users\Mihawk (src/pw_wine_profile.h moves an older steamuser one) */
+    static const char steamuserA[] = "Mihawk";
     if(*size < ARRAY_SIZE(steamuserA)){
         SetLastError( ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_BUFFER );
         *size = ARRAY_SIZE(steamuserA);
@@ -60,7 +61,7 @@
  */
 BOOL WINAPI GetUserNameW( LPWSTR name, LPDWORD size )
 {
-    static const WCHAR steamuserW[] = {'s','t','e','a','m','u','s','e','r',0};
+    static const WCHAR steamuserW[] = L"Mihawk";
     if(*size < ARRAY_SIZE(steamuserW)){
         SetLastError( ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_BUFFER );
         *size = ARRAY_SIZE(steamuserW);
